BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
AT MADURAI

CASE NO: C.R.P.\(MD\) No. 1290 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD010567892026
DECISION DATE: 2026-01-15
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar

PARTIES:
Subramanian and Another \(Defendants 1 & 2\)
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
Pitchaiammal and 4 others \(Plaintiffs\)
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Code of Civil Procedure 1908, Limitation Act 1963

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
CPC Order VII Rule 11\(d\), Limitation Act Article 58, CPC Section 115

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Rejection of Plaint, Order VII Rule 11, Barred by Limitation, Clever Drafting, Civil Revision

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Suit for declaration of title filed 18 years after registered partition deed. Defendants filed application under Order VII Rule 11\(d\) CPC to reject plaint as barred by limitation.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Whether meaningful reading of plaint demonstrates suit is barred by limitation despite clever drafting?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Applying Dahiben v. Arvindbhai Kalyanji Bhanusali: Plaint must be rejected if averments show claim is barred by limitation without trial.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Where averments in plaint read as a whole disclose that right to sue accrued beyond 3 years under Article 58 Limitation Act, plaint is liable to rejection under Order VII Rule 11\(d\) CPC.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Civil Revision Petition Allowed; Order of Trial Court set aside; Plaint rejected under Order VII Rule 11\(d\) CPC as barred by limitation.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice R. Vijayakumar
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
